    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d373">

                <pb facs="0452" n="440" sameAs="frus:frus1942v01/pg440"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">390.1115A/1006: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Lourenço Marques</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Preston</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lourenço Marques</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-07-28">July 28, 1942</date>.<lb/>[Received July 28—6
                        p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>192. From MacGowan [and] Nicol<anchor n="61" xml:id="d373-f1"/> for Gehan.<anchor
                        n="62" xml:id="d373-f2"/></p>
                <p>“<hi rendition="#italic">Gripsholm</hi> arrived 20th, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Conte</hi> [and?] <hi rendition="#italic">Asama</hi> 22d. Exchange
                    operation accomplished 24th successfully under 4 hours. However, considerable
                    confusion berthing, originally based lists our possession prior arrival
                    necessitating complete reberthing program after exchange effected based on
                    steamers official lists. Reberthing work terminated evening 26th. Order avoid
                    similar extremely unpleasant <pb facs="0453" n="441" xml:id="pg441"/> occurrence
                    which serious, necessary you arrange we return New York [as soon as possible]
                    order report and rectify system exchange which otherwise perfect. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Gripsholm</hi> sailed 28th, 1,510 aboard, details later.
                    Your 6, yes.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Preston</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d373-f1" n="61" xml:id="d373-f1-content">
                <p>John MacGowan and Robert Nicol of American Export Lines.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d373-f2" n="62" xml:id="d373-f2-content">
                <p>John F. Gehan, vice president of American Export Lines.</p>
